# Bloatmaw kit — the HARD half of the character: the shackles and their
# snapped chain. Authored in WAM; the flesh is characters/bloatmaw.blob.
#
# WHY MESH AND NOT SDF. Two concrete reasons, both the format's own:
#   1. `clearOf` samples a primitive's shaft spaced to its own effective
#      radius and warns above length/effRadius 32 that a real crossing can be
#      stepped over and reported as a false "clear". A chain link is exactly
#      that slender shape.
#   2. One cluster may not exceed 64 primitives (MAX_CLUSTER_PRIMS). A chain
#      eats that budget fast and the constant must not be raised.
# So the flesh owns the ball, maw, teeth, eyes and arms; the kit owns only the
# iron around the wrists.
#
# THE SKELETON BELOW IS A HAND TRANSCRIPTION OF bloatmaw.blob AND NOTHING
# CHECKS THAT THEY STAY IN STEP. Two conversions apply, neither optional:
#   * UNITS. WAM lengths are fractions of `height`; .blob's are metres. Every
#     number here is the .blob metre value / 1.83.
#   * PITCH SIGN ON `down` BONES. WAM's pitch tips an `up` bone forward and a
#     `down` bone BACKWARD; .blob's always carries toward +z. So `up` bones
#     share their pitch verbatim and every `down` bone NEGATES it. This kit
#     only needs the forearm/wrist chain right, since that is all it hangs
#     from — but the whole arm chain is transcribed because a missing link in
#     the chain would put the cuff on the wrong side of the wrist.
# The .blob root is a BONE with a length (`root pelvis at 1.08 len=0.06`), and
# children attach at its TAIL; WAM's root is a bare point, so `hips` carries
# that missing 0.06 m and every .blob `parent=pelvis` becomes `parent=hips`.
#
# BUILD:  scripts/build-wam-kit.sh bloatmaw
#   -> public/assets/lab/bloatmaw-kit.gltf
model bloatmaw-kit
  height 1.83
  style chunky

palette
  iron #4d5157
  brass #8a6a34

skeleton
  root pelvis at 0.590164
  # The .blob root bone's own length (0.06 m), restored as a real segment.
  bone hips   parent=pelvis dir=up len=0.032787
  # Only the chain that leads to the wrist is needed; the .blob spine, neck,
  # skull and maw carry no kit geometry and are omitted deliberately.
  bone spine  parent=hips dir=up len=0.163934
  mirror
    # .blob: dir=down tilt=63, no pitch -> WAM pitch 0, tilt verbatim.
    bone clavicle parent=spine dir=down tilt=63 len=0.387978
    bone upperArm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=60 len=0.071038
    # .blob pitch +8 -> WAM -8 (see the header).
    bone foreArm  parent=upperArm dir=down tilt=50 pitch=-8 len=0.060109
    # .blob pitch +10 -> WAM -10.
    bone hand     parent=foreArm dir=down tilt=45 pitch=-10 len=0.038251
  end

parts
  mirror
    # SHACKLE — a riveted iron cuff around the wrist. Three rings sized off
    # the flesh it wraps: the .blob forearm tapers to r2=0.028 at the wrist
    # and the palm blob (r 0.044 x wide 1.15 = 0.051 in x) is just past it,
    # so a 0.062 half-width sits ~1 cm proud of the cuff's own section without
    # swallowing the hand. Open at both ends (`cap none`): a flat cap would
    # put a disc through the wrist, which is the goblin's greave lesson.
    loft shackle bones=hand..hand material=iron
      ring 0.02 w=0.056 d=0.056
      ring 0.16 w=0.064 d=0.064
      ring 0.30 w=0.058 d=0.058
      cap start=none end=none

    # SNAPPED CHAIN — three links hanging free and short. The brief is
    # explicit that the chain does NOT loop, coil, or connect to anything, so
    # this is a straight three-link dangle: no last link reaching back to the
    # cuff, no second strand. Each link is a short flattened tube and the
    # `roll=90` alternation on every other link is what makes a row of tubes
    # read as CHAIN rather than as a rod — the flat faces turn a quarter turn
    # at each joint, exactly as real links do.
    loft chain1 bone=hand at=0.30 offset=(0.040,-0.035,0) dir=down len=0.028 material=iron
      ring 0.06 w=0.020 d=0.007
      ring 0.94 w=0.020 d=0.007
      cap start=none end=none
    loft chain2 bone=hand at=0.30 offset=(0.040,-0.065,0) dir=down len=0.028 material=iron
      ring 0.06 w=0.020 d=0.007 roll=90
      ring 0.94 w=0.020 d=0.007 roll=90
      cap start=none end=none
    loft chain3 bone=hand at=0.30 offset=(0.040,-0.095,0) dir=down len=0.028 material=iron
      ring 0.06 w=0.020 d=0.007
      ring 0.94 w=0.020 d=0.007
      cap start=none end=none

    # The snapped end: a torn stub link half the length of the others, so the
    # chain reads as BROKEN rather than merely short.
    loft chain4 bone=hand at=0.30 offset=(0.040,-0.124,0) dir=down len=0.014 material=brass
      ring 0.10 w=0.018 d=0.006 roll=90
      ring 0.90 w=0.014 d=0.005 roll=90
      cap start=none end=none
  end
